.TH SKYAPO 1 "2026-09-30" "SkyAPO 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
skyapo \- control the SkyAPO audio processing daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skyapo
.I command
[\fIarguments\fR]
.br
.B skyapo --help
.br
.B skyapo --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B skyapo
is the command-line client for SkyAPO. The daemon and the audio graph run as
the current user; no root service is required. Commands that query or control
the running graph communicate with the per-user daemon.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print the daemon and audio graph status. If the daemon is unavailable, the
status output says so.
.TP
.B diagnostics [--json]
Print build/runtime diagnostics. With \fB--json\fR, emit machine-readable
JSON; unavailable runtime fields are represented as \fBnull\fR.
.TP
.B start | stop | restart
Start, stop, or restart the per-user daemon. Start waits for PipeWire format
negotiation and requires a selected capture device.
.TP
.B device list
List PipeWire capture devices, including stable node names and available
channel/sample-rate metadata.
.TP
.B device set \fIid-or-name\fR
Select a capture device. The selection is persisted by stable node name;
numeric PipeWire IDs are accepted for the current selection operation only.
.TP
.B device current
Print the selected capture device.
.TP
.B config show
Print the daemon's active configuration file.
.TP
.B config check \fIfile\fR
Validate a configuration using the current CLI validation format.
.TP
.B config check --json \fIfile\fR
Validate a configuration and print a JSON result to standard output. Exit
status is zero for a valid configuration and nonzero for an invalid one.
.TP
.B config reload
Ask the daemon to validate and transactionally reload its active configuration.
.TP
.B filters
Print the active filter chain. Requires a running daemon.
.TP
.B plugin list
List plugins discoverable by the plugin hosts built into this package.
.TP
.B plugin info \fIURI\fR
Print metadata for a discovered plugin.
.TP
.B plugin set \fIPLUGIN-ID\fR \fIPARAM\fR \fIVALUE\fR
Set a live parameter on the uniquely matching active plugin instance. Current
hosts validate the parameter against the plugin's declared range and deliver
the update at an audio block boundary; the update is not persisted to the
configuration file. Parameter identifiers and value units depend on format.
.TP
.B plugin bypass \fIPLUGIN-ID\fR on|off
Enable or disable SkyAPO's transparent host bypass for the uniquely matching
active LV2, CLAP, or VST3 plugin instance. The state is runtime-only. Bypass
copies plugin input to output without calling the plugin process hook.
.TP
.B help, --help, -h
Print command help.
.TP
.B --version
Print the SkyAPO version and pinned Equalizer APO upstream revision.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/skyapo
Per-user configuration directory. If \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is unset,
SkyAPO uses \fI~/.config/skyapo\fR.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/skyapo.sock
Mode-0600 per-user daemon control socket.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Selects the per-user configuration root.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Selects the per-user runtime directory containing the daemon socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR skyapod (1),
.BR pw-cli (1),
.BR wpctl (1)
